Z||000000||I wish I had a GT||06-26-2001||02:50 PM||||my 87 coupe backfires, my guess is the timing is off. It starts up very rough and sometimes stalls while starting.  It won't backfire if I accelerate REALLY slowly (0-60 in about 5 min)and I can feel it about to backfire usually and prevent it by letting off the gass for a couple seconds and then once again SLOWLY accelerating.  Is it probably the timing? whats wrong and how do I fix it?  any help and oppions would be great||||reg||8
Z||000001||SteveJ||06-26-2001||03:00 PM||||Yea it does sound like timing. But first, did you do any maintenance just before this problem occurred? Like remove any spark plug wires?||||reg||1
